{"evidence":[{"pdf_page":81,"quote":"Circularity and reuse is one of the key measures in NCC\u2019s Climate Transition Plan. This entails a focus on materials selection and design together with customers to meet requirements for lower climate impact, decreased use of materials and reduced use of virgin materials as a resource. This is described in more detail in section E1 on pp. 66\u201375.","source_id":"KB-B030-NCC-ASR2025"}],"knowledge_status":"reference_candidate","predicate":{"canonical_key":"evidence_snippet_circularity","raw_key":"circularity"},"promotion":{"eligible":false,"reason":"requires_atomic_projection_and_independent_evidence_gate"},"provenance":{"reference_status":"mineru_exact_quote_pending_semantic_projection","simulated":false,"source_artifact":"artifacts/scale_batch_030/mineru_targets_RESUME02/KB-B030-NCC-ASR2025-p0081/ncc-annual-and-sustainability-report-2025/auto/ncc-annual-and-sustainability-report-2025.md","source_sha256":"7ae12a0f22ea10f38fc3356e126658da30a4ff8ae117a03a9aced359b2500c02"},"qualifiers":{"answer_status":"unverified_evidence_candidate","calculation_expression":null,"normalized_unit":null,"period_literal":"2025","reference_period":2025,"scope_boundary":null,"value_origin":"issuer_disclosure_extracted"},"record_id":"fact-a6c1e787fabdcf04ef3d2179","record_kind":"fact","schema_version":"0.1","subject":{"document_ids":["KB-B030-NCC-ASR2025"],"document_metadata":[{"company":"NCC AB (publ)","document_id":"KB-B030-NCC-ASR2025","language":"English","local_path":"data/raw/scale_batch_030/ncc-annual-and-sustainability-report-2025.pdf","sha256":"253f5b9bf6a12ec5ce7e1965711dcda91af42da1bd58cb37972b5d87af853de2","title":"NCC Annual and Sustainability Report 2025"}],"entity_label":"NCC AB (publ)","task_id":"KB-B028-KB-B030-NCC-ASR2025-P0081-CIRCULARITY-1"},"trust_tier":"C","value":"Circularity and reuse is one of the key measures in NCC\u2019s Climate Transition Plan. This entails a focus on materials selection and design together with customers to meet requirements for lower climate impact, decreased use of materials and reduced use of virgin materials as a resource. This is described in more detail in section E1 on pp. 66\u201375."}
{"evidence":[{"pdf_page":81,"quote":"Resource outflow concerns in part the buildings and structures that NCC produces, and in part the waste and residual materials that arise in production and how these are handled, recycled or reused. The ambition is to minimize the amount of waste going to incineration or landfill and instead creating circular flows where materials can be reused in new projects. These efforts cover both construction and demolition waste as well as internal processes for sorting and recycling, and cooperation with external waste operators. The products that NCC manufactures have a long service life and are repairable and recyclable, and the majority of the materials purchased end up in these products. Of the total inflow of materials, waste amounts to only 1 percent.","source_id":"KB-B030-NCC-ASR2025"}],"knowledge_status":"reference_candidate","predicate":{"canonical_key":"evidence_snippet_circularity","raw_key":"circularity"},"promotion":{"eligible":false,"reason":"requires_atomic_projection_and_independent_evidence_gate"},"provenance":{"reference_status":"mineru_exact_quote_pending_semantic_projection","simulated":false,"source_artifact":"artifacts/scale_batch_030/mineru_targets_RESUME02/KB-B030-NCC-ASR2025-p0081/ncc-annual-and-sustainability-report-2025/auto/ncc-annual-and-sustainability-report-2025.md","source_sha256":"7ae12a0f22ea10f38fc3356e126658da30a4ff8ae117a03a9aced359b2500c02"},"qualifiers":{"answer_status":"unverified_evidence_candidate","calculation_expression":null,"normalized_unit":null,"period_literal":"2025","reference_period":2025,"scope_boundary":null,"value_origin":"issuer_disclosure_extracted"},"record_id":"fact-0707f13e156883002493e3c2","record_kind":"fact","schema_version":"0.1","subject":{"document_ids":["KB-B030-NCC-ASR2025"],"document_metadata":[{"company":"NCC AB (publ)","document_id":"KB-B030-NCC-ASR2025","language":"English","local_path":"data/raw/scale_batch_030/ncc-annual-and-sustainability-report-2025.pdf","sha256":"253f5b9bf6a12ec5ce7e1965711dcda91af42da1bd58cb37972b5d87af853de2","title":"NCC Annual and Sustainability Report 2025"}],"entity_label":"NCC AB (publ)","task_id":"KB-B028-KB-B030-NCC-ASR2025-P0081-CIRCULARITY-2"},"trust_tier":"C","value":"Resource outflow concerns in part the buildings and structures that NCC produces, and in part the waste and residual materials that arise in production and how these are handled, recycled or reused. The ambition is to minimize the amount of waste going to incineration or landfill and instead creating circular flows where materials can be reused in new projects. These efforts cover both construction and demolition waste as well as internal processes for sorting and recycling, and cooperation with external waste operators. The products that NCC manufactures have a long service life and are repairable and recyclable, and the majority of the materials purchased end up in these products. Of the total inflow of materials, waste amounts to only 1 percent."}
{"evidence":[{"pdf_page":85,"quote":"To support effective governance, NCC works in accordance with ISO\u00a045001, which is linked to occupational health and safety. Currently, significant parts of the operational units are certified in accordance with ISO 45001, or intend to be certified. Internal audits are conducted continuously, while units that are ISO 45001 certified are also audited externally.","source_id":"KB-B030-NCC-ASR2025"}],"knowledge_status":"reference_candidate","predicate":{"canonical_key":"evidence_snippet_health_safety","raw_key":"health_safety"},"promotion":{"eligible":false,"reason":"requires_atomic_projection_and_independent_evidence_gate"},"provenance":{"reference_status":"mineru_exact_quote_pending_semantic_projection","simulated":false,"source_artifact":"artifacts/scale_batch_030/mineru_targets_RESUME02/KB-B030-NCC-ASR2025-p0085/ncc-annual-and-sustainability-report-2025/auto/ncc-annual-and-sustainability-report-2025.md","source_sha256":"950de9769f5ea739380e91b6eef954099a390206c9675b01dbd5a68424ae3cea"},"qualifiers":{"answer_status":"unverified_evidence_candidate","calculation_expression":null,"normalized_unit":null,"period_literal":"2025","reference_period":2025,"scope_boundary":null,"value_origin":"issuer_disclosure_extracted"},"record_id":"fact-c9f85301228d7b2b1ebd496c","record_kind":"fact","schema_version":"0.1","subject":{"document_ids":["KB-B030-NCC-ASR2025"],"document_metadata":[{"company":"NCC AB (publ)","document_id":"KB-B030-NCC-ASR2025","language":"English","local_path":"data/raw/scale_batch_030/ncc-annual-and-sustainability-report-2025.pdf","sha256":"253f5b9bf6a12ec5ce7e1965711dcda91af42da1bd58cb37972b5d87af853de2","title":"NCC Annual and Sustainability Report 2025"}],"entity_label":"NCC AB (publ)","task_id":"KB-B028-KB-B030-NCC-ASR2025-P0085-HEALTH_SAFETY-1"},"trust_tier":"C","value":"To support effective governance, NCC works in accordance with ISO\u00a045001, which is linked to occupational health and safety. Currently, significant parts of the operational units are certified in accordance with ISO 45001, or intend to be certified. Internal audits are conducted continuously, while units that are ISO 45001 certified are also audited externally."}
